  "chapter": {
    "bookTitle": "Genesis",
    "delineation": "Chapter",
    "number": 34,
    "summary": "Shechem defiles Dinah—The Hivites seek to arrange marriages with Jacob’s family—Many, having been circumcised, are slain by Simeon and Levi—Jacob reproves his sons.",
    "chapterAugmentations": [],
    "verses": [
      {
        "text": "And Dinah the daughter of Leah, which she bare unto Jacob, went out to see the daughters of the land.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 1,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:1",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 1
      },
      {
        "text": "And when Shechem the son of Hamor the Hivite, prince of the country, saw her, he took her, and lay with her, and defiled her.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 28,
            "end": 33,
            "text": "Judg. 9:28."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 2,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Judg. 9:28.",
            "prettyString": "Judges 9:28",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "judges",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 9,
                    "end": 9,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 28,
                        "end": 28
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:2",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 2
      },
      {
        "text": "And his soul clave unto Dinah the daughter of Jacob, and he loved the damsel, and spake kindly unto the damsel.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 3,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:3",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 3
      },
      {
        "text": "And Shechem spake unto his father Hamor, saying, Get me this damsel to wife.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 4,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:4",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 4
      },
      {
        "text": "And Jacob heard that he had defiled Dinah his daughter: now his sons were with his cattle in the field: and Jacob held his peace until they were come.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 5,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:5",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 5
      },
      {
        "text": "And Hamor the father of Shechem went out unto Jacob to commune with him.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 6,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:6",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 6
      },
      {
        "text": "And the sons of Jacob came out of the field when they heard it: and the men were grieved, and they were very wroth, because he had wrought folly in Israel in lying with Jacob’s daughter; which thing ought not to be done.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 109,
            "end": 114,
            "text": "Gen. 49:7."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 60,
            "end": 63
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 7,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Gen. 49:7.",
            "prettyString": "Genesis 49:7",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "genesis",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 49,
                    "end": 49,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 7,
                        "end": 7
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:7",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 7
      },
      {
        "text": "And Hamor communed with them, saying, The soul of my son Shechem longeth for your daughter: I pray you give her him to wife.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 8,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:8",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 8
      },
      {
        "text": "And make ye marriages with us, and give your daughters unto us, and take our daughters unto you.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 31,
            "end": 34
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 9,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:9",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 9
      },
      {
        "text": "And ye shall dwell with us: and the land shall be before you; dwell and trade ye therein, and get you possessions therein.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 36,
            "end": 40,
            "text": "Gen. 20:15."
          },
          {
            "start": 72,
            "end": 77,
