        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:10",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 10
      },
      {
        "text": "And Shechem said unto her father and unto her brethren, Let me find grace in your eyes, and what ye shall say unto me I will give.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 11,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:11",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 11
      },
      {
        "text": "Ask me never so much dowry and gift, and I will give according as ye shall say unto me: but give me the damsel to wife.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 7,
            "end": 26,
            "text": "OR ever so high a dowry."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 12,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:12",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 12
      },
      {
        "text": "And the sons of Jacob answered Shechem and Hamor his father deceitfully, and said, because he had defiled Dinah their sister:",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 13,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:13",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 13
      },
      {
        "text": "And they said unto them, We cannot do this thing, to give our sister to one that is uncircumcised; for that were a reproach unto us:",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 3,
            "text": "Septuagint: And Simeon and Levi, brothers of Dinah, sons of Leah, said …"
          },
          {
            "start": 84,
            "end": 97,
            "text": "Judg. 14:3."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 108,
            "end": 112
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 14,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Judg. 14:3.",
            "prettyString": "Judges 14:3",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "judges",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 14,
                    "end": 14,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 3,
                        "end": 3
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:14",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 14
      },
      {
        "text": "But in this will we consent unto you: If ye will be as we be, that every male of you be circumcised;",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 88,
            "end": 99,
            "text": "TG Circumcision."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 58,
            "end": 61
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 15,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "TG Circumcision.",
            "prettyString": "TG Circumcision",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "studyHelp",
                "studyHelpType": "tg",
                "title": "Circumcision",
                "entryId": "tg-circumcision",
                "book": "",
                "chapters": []
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:15",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 15
      },
      {
        "text": "Then will we give our daughters unto you, and we will take your daughters to us, and we will dwell with you, and we will become one people.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 16,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:16",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 16
      },
      {
        "text": "But if ye will not hearken unto us, to be circumcised; then will we take our daughter, and we will be gone.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 17,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:17",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 17
      },
      {
        "text": "And their words pleased Hamor, and Shechem Hamor’s son.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 18,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:18",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 18
      },
      {
        "text": "And the young man deferred not to do the thing, because he had delight in Jacob’s daughter: and he was more honourable than all the house of his father.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 99,
            "end": 102
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 19,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:19",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 19
      },
      {
        "text": "And Hamor and Shechem his son came unto the gate of their city, and communed with the men of their city, saying,",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 44,
            "end": 48,
            "text": "Gen. 23:10."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 20,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Gen. 23:10.",
            "prettyString": "Genesis 23:10",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "genesis",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 23,
                    "end": 23,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 10,
                        "end": 10
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:20",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 20
      },
      {
        "text": "These men are peaceable with us; therefore let them dwell in the land, and trade therein; for the land, behold, it is large enough for them; let us take their daughters to us for wives, and let us give them our daughters.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 10,
            "end": 13
          },
          {
            "start": 112,
            "end": 117
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 21,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:21",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 21
      },
      {
        "text": "Only herein will the men consent unto us for to dwell with us, to be one people, if every male among us be circumcised, as they are circumcised.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 128,
            "end": 131
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 22,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:22",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 22
      },
      {
        "text": "Shall not their cattle and their substance and every beast of theirs be ours? only let us consent unto them, and they will dwell with us.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 0,
            "end": 5
          },
          {
            "start": 69,
            "end": 71
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 23,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:23",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 23
      },
      {
        "text": "And unto Hamor and unto Shechem his son hearkened all that went out of the gate of his city; and every male was circumcised, all that went out of the gate of his city.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 24,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:24",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 24
      },
      {
        "text": "And it came to pass on the third day, when they were sore, that two of the sons of Jacob, Simeon and Levi, Dinah’s brethren, took each man his sword, and came upon the city boldly, and slew all the males.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 90,
            "end": 96,
            "text": "Gen. 49:5 (5–7)."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 25,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:25",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 25
      },
      {
        "text": "And they slew Hamor and Shechem his son with the edge of the sword, and took Dinah out of Shechem’s house, and went out.",
        "footNotes": [
          {
            "start": 9,
            "end": 13,
            "text": "Gen. 49:6."
          }
        ],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 26,
        "crossReferences": [
          {
            "raw": "Gen. 49:6.",
            "prettyString": "Genesis 49:6",
            "references": [
              {
                "type": "scripture",
                "book": "genesis",
                "chapters": [
                  {
                    "start": 49,
                    "end": 49,
                    "verses": [
                      {
                        "start": 6,
                        "end": 6
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:26",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 26
      },
      {
        "text": "The sons of Jacob came upon the slain, and spoiled the city, because they had defiled their sister.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 27,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:27",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 27
      },
      {
        "text": "They took their sheep, and their oxen, and their asses, and that which was in the city, and that which was in the field,",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 71,
            "end": 74
          },
          {
            "start": 103,
            "end": 106
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 28,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:28",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 28
      },
      {
        "text": "And all their wealth, and all their little ones, and their wives took they captive, and spoiled even all that was in the house.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 110,
            "end": 113
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 29,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:29",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 29
      },
      {
        "text": "And Jacob said to Simeon and Levi, Ye have troubled me to make me to stink among the inhabitants of the land, among the Canaanites and the Perizzites: and I being few in number, they shall gather themselves together against me, and slay me; and I shall be destroyed, I and my house.",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [
          {
            "start": 157,
            "end": 162
          }
        ],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 30,
        "crossReferences": [],
        "jstReferences": [],
        "reference": "Genesis 34:30",
        "book": "Genesis",
        "chapter": 34,
        "verse": 30
      },
      {
        "text": "And they said, Should he deal with our sister as with an harlot?",
        "footNotes": [],
        "italics": [],
        "associatedContent": [],
        "verseNumber": 31,
        "crossReferences": [],
